<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia buys 150,000 T U.S. wheat -trade.</title>
<headline>Tunisia buys 150,000 T U.S. wheat -trade.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia purchased six lots of 25,000 tonnes each of U.S. origin wheat at between $148.21 and $159.95 per tonne C&amp;F for August to October shipment at a tender on Friday, buyers told Reuters.</p>
<p>Details-</p>
<p> 25,000 tonnes   10-20 August HRW NR2  $159.95 C&amp;F</p>
<p> 25,000 tonnes   20-31 Aug    SRW NR2  $148.44 C&amp;F</p>
<p> 25,000 tonnes   01-10 Sept   HRW NR2  $159.44 C&amp;F</p>
<p> 25,000 tonnes   10-20 Sept   SRW NR2  $151.05 C&amp;F</p>
<p> 25,000 tonnes   20-30 Sept   HRW NR2  $159.44 C&amp;F</p>
<p> 25,000 tonnes   01-10 Oct    SRW NR2  $148.21 C&amp;F</p>
<p>Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
